From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 02:46:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] docs: record the disconnected feasible set on the frozen
 interface

The full 42-cell grid on the one rescuable persistent-failure seed completes
14 cells, and the successes fall into two separated regions with failure
between and inside them: 3/7 at a pure inertial hold, 0/7 one step in, then
5/7 and 5/7 at the two staging radii nearest the offline plan's, then 0/7
closer still. Interpolating between two working settings lands in the hole.

That non-convexity is the strongest available argument for a learned upper
layer, and it rules out reading the result as a retuned setpoint. The best
cell completes in 122.1 s where the earlier interface needed 271.2 s.

