From 0405efd67bbb79f7c9b2d51a39fa7eed55ebd6dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 03:37:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat: add the per-decision replay diagnostic and the T8
 execution order

The T7 monitor keeps one row per episode, which shows that two of four seeds
run the clock out but not how they do it. replay_hybrid_policy.py runs a
checkpoint deterministically and records, per decision, the commanded action,
true range, reference radius, geometry margins, entry events, feedback
summary, fallback count and the termination flags -- and prints the fraction
of decisions whose commit channel sits on the negative half, which is the
directly falsifiable form of the T7 hypothesis that the dead seeds simply
learned to wait. It is read-only and changes no configuration.

The execution order covers the formal twelve-seed evaluation of all four
checkpoints plus the fixed-setpoint control row, the third training seed each
version needs to meet the three-seed rule, the paired dead-versus-live
replay, and a one-off timing breakdown of the decision cost. It keeps all
four seeds including the two that complete nothing, and it stops rather than
improvising if the replay falsifies the waiting hypothesis.

